        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "510e8d0c-0103-5683-b7d5-4f85c94f372f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Psalter of Bonne de Luxembourg\n- People: Bonne de Luxembourg, John the Blind, John II of France, Jean Le Noir\n- Places: The Cloisters, New York\n- Roles: Duchess of Normandy, Count of Luxembourg, King of Bohemia, titular King of Poland\n\nFacts:\n- John the Blind was born on 10 August 1296 and died on 26 August 1346.\n- John the Blind was Count of Luxembourg from 1309, King of Bohemia from 1310, and titular King of Poland.\n- The Psalter of Bonne de Luxembourg is a small 14th-century illuminated manuscript made in tempera, grisaille, ink, and gold leaf on vellum.\n- The Psalter of Bonne de Luxembourg was probably executed for Bonne de Luxembourg, Duchess of Normandy, around 1348–1349 near the end of her husband John II of France’s life.\n- Bonne de Luxembourg was the daughter of John the Blind and the wife of John II of France.\n- Jean Le Noir’s main work is the Psalter of Bonne de Luxembourg, dated about 1348–1349.\n- The Psalter of Bonne de Luxembourg is now in the collection of The Cloisters in New York.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
